WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.320
Take butter and olive oil
from the same cupboard.

2
00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:06.770
One is a solid block; the other pours.

3
00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:09.760
Yet both are made of the
same kind of molecule:

4
00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:13.000
one glycerol joined to three fatty acids.

5
00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:17.350
Weight for weight, they release about
twice as much energy as carbohydrate.

6
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:22.400
So why is one solid and the other runny,
when their molecules are the same kind?

7
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:25.860
In this mission, you'll see how
a triglyceride is assembled,

8
00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:28.500
and why lipids keep apart from water.

9
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:32.320
Then you'll compare saturated
and unsaturated fatty acids,

10
00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:35.160
and read four melting points from a graph.

11
00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:39.760
Your mission: explain why butter
is solid but olive oil runs,

12
00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:42.110
though both are the same kind of molecule.
